<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44713" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐπᾰτρίδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔπαρ-δας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατήρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of good or
				noble sire, of noble family</i>, of persons, used by Trag. in
			lyr., <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				162
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				920
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				152
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. οἶκοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ion</u>
					1073
				</span></i>
			: also in later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Muson.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				13
			</span></i>B<i><span class="en">
				p.69
			</span></i> H. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὐ., οἱ</span>,
			at Athens, the <i>old aristocracy</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγροῖκοι</span> (or 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεωμόροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Thes.</u>
					25
				</span></i>
			) and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημιουργοί</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				13.2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Scol.</u>
				14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				16.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				8.40
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πένητας Εὐπατρίδας οὐδεὶς ὁρᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					90.3
				</span></i>
			; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ τῶν Εὐ. πάτρια</span>
			sacred traditions of the <u>Eup.</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				9.410a
			</span></i> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξηγητὴς ἐξ Εὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.267
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1335
			</span></i>, refer to a particular family of that name. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> at Rome, <u>Patricians</u>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Publ.</u>
				18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fab.</u>
				16
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
